<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meluhha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Meluḫḫa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Meluhha was a land known to ancient Mesopotamians, generally identified with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus-valley-civilisation">Indus Valley civilisation</a>. It was reached by sea through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> and supplied goods such as carnelian, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> and other luxuries. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>'s control of the Gulf trade gave it access to Meluhha's products.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meluhha.jpg" alt="Meluhha" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Middle_East_topographic_map-blank.svg: Sémhur (talk) derivative work: Zunkir (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moyen_Orient_3mil_aC.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
